export anchor FiftiesDinerStyle:
    number: 51
    screen: Pricing
    name: 50s diner
    idea: A retro American diner menu in cherry red and mint, with script headings, a checkerboard band, chrome trim and dotted price leaders that make choosing a plan feel like ordering lunch.
    base: light
    palette:
        cream: #fffaf0, the page
        vanilla: #fff3dc, the menu card and the table caption
        cherry: #c41e3a, script titles, prices, the primary button and the table head
        cherryShade: #8f1028, the pressed lip under red buttons
        mint: #a8e6cf, the header band, the free months note and the title shadow
        mintPale: #dff5ec, the featured plan, striped rows and the style sheet
        teal: #1d6b55, small capital labels, the secondary button and tick discs
        cocoa: #3a2e2a, body text, outlines and the checkerboard
        cocoaSoft: #6a5a52, italic notes and captions
        chrome: #fbfcfd to #c9d0d7 to #8e98a3 to #dfe4e9, a vertical gradient for the menu rim and the toggle track
    type:
        Script is Brush Script MT, Segoe Script, Snell Roundhand, Lucida
        Handwriting, cursive, set italic. Sans is Futura, Century Gothic,
        Avenir Next, Trebuchet MS, sans-serif. The title is 96px script
        with a 3px mint offset shadow, section titles 52 to 56px script,
        plan names 28px extra bold capitals, prices 40px extra bold, body
        17px on a 1.5 line, and labels 13px bold capitals at 0.14em.
    layout:
        A mint header band with a red star badge logo, the brand in script
        and pill nav links, closed by a cocoa and cream checkerboard band
        between cherry lines. A centred hero holds the script title, a teal
        tagline, a short line and a chrome pill toggle beside a mint 2
        months free pill. The plans sit in one menu card with a chrome rim
        and rounded corners. Each plan is a menu line, the name in capitals,
        a dotted leader and the price at the right, then the billing words,
        the features joined by red bullets and a pill button. Team is a mint
        panel inside the menu with a red starburst reading Most popular.
        Then a rounded white comparison card with a red head and mint
        striped rows, questions as speech bubbles with a red Q disc, and a
        checkerboard band above the footer. Below 720px menu lines wrap
        and buttons drop under the features.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between menu items, 36 to 40px card padding and 72px between sections.
    density: Medium. Plans read as stacked menu lines, not cards side by side.
    corners: Round. 28px menu rim, 20px table card, 16px swatches, fully round pills and buttons, and speech bubbles with one sharp corner.
    borders: 2px cocoa outlines, dotted leaders and dividers, a double cherry rule under the menu title and the checkerboard bands.
    shadows: One soft drop under the menu, 0 10px 24px at 18 percent cocoa. A hard mint offset behind the table. Red buttons carry an inset cherryShade lip and a white then grey chrome ring.
    icons:
        Few and sign-like. A star badge logo, a starburst for Most
        popular, white ticks in filled teal circles, a Q disc on each
        question, a tick on the chosen billing option and plus and minus
        toggles.
    focus: A 3px dashed cherry outline offset 4px. A focused field gets a white gap and then a 2px cherry ring.
    tone: Warm counter talk, such as Today's plans, Ask the counter and What comes on each plate.
